.TH CCO 1 "2026-11-20" "cco 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cco \- scaffold C projects that build with the cco build runtime
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cco
.B new
.I path
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B cco
.B init
.RI [ path ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cco
is the C11 counterpart of
.BR cco++ (1).
It generates a project whose build description is the build tool: a
.B build.c
that includes the single header
.B cco.h
and drives compilation, linking, tests and
.B compile_commands.json
generation itself.
.PP
The scaffold writes
.BR build.c ,
.BR cco.h ,
.BR README.md ,
.BR compile_flags.txt ,
.B .gitignore
and either
.B src/main.c
or, with
.BR \-\-lib ,
a library layout with
.BR include/ ,
.B src/
and
.BR tests/ .
.PP
The generated
.B build
program has its own command line: run
.B ./build \-\-help
for its subcommands and options. The build API it exposes is documented in
.I c/API.md
in the cco source tree.
.PP
Invoking
.B cco
with no arguments or with unknown options prints its usage summary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-bin
Generate an executable project. This is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-lib
Generate a library project, with a test target linked against it.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " name"
Target name. Defaults to the directory name.
.TP
.B \-\-build
Compile
.B build.c
and run it once after scaffolding.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite scaffold files that already exist. Files under
.BR src/ ,
.B include/
and
.B tests/
are not touched.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress per-file output and the suggested next steps.
.TP
.BI \-\-cco-header " path"
Header to vendor. Use it when
.B cco.h
does not sit next to the
.B cco
executable or under
.BR ../include/cco/ .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B build.c
Generated build description. It is the build tool; there is no Makefile.
.TP
.B cco.h
Runtime header written into the project root, copied from the installation
the scaffold found.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CC
Compiler driver used by generated builds when
.B \-\-cc
is not given.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cco++ (1),
.BR cc (1)
.PP
The API used by a generated
.B build.c
is documented in
.I c/API.md
in the cco source tree.
